// `#[Transient]` says something about a **field** — that it is not part of its type's serialized
// shape — so it attaches to nothing else. The restriction is what makes a misplaced one visible: an
// attribute nobody reads at a site is silent, not wrong-looking, so `#[Transient]` on a function
// would otherwise check clean, run clean, and mean nothing at all.
//
// It is the ordinary placement gate (E0030), the same one an `@attribute(Field)` record of your own
// gets — std's attributes declare their sites through the same channel rather than a rule of their
// own, and the diagnostic names them: it is restricted to Field.
// expect: error E0030 at 14:3
// expect: error E0030 at 17:3
// expect: exit 1
use std.json.Transient

#[Transient]
fn helper(): int { return 1; }

#[Transient]
struct Order { id: string }

echo helper();
